      "mergeID": "62fea58ba9b61a44b287c6f4",
      "mergedPostDetails": "# Issue:\nIn bright worlds you basically can't even see your gesture icons once they faded out. They get way to transparent for you to be able to see them.\n# Suggestion:\nThe behavior could be improved in to ways:\n1. Don't fade them out so much.\n2. Give them a different color.\nA combination out of the two would probably be the best. Not letting them fade out so much should already help a lot, but also giving them a different color would probably improve the visibility even more. It would allow you to see them better in brighter / white worlds.\nAnother way I could see this being solved is by giving it out lines. This could improve visibility quiet a lot as well.\n# Attachments:\nHere you can see that the faded out ones are basically invisible. (I'm doing a fist with both hands and they are already faded out)",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1222] Gesture Icons fade out too much / are hard to see when faded out",
